  "text": "\r\n\t\t Student Voting | Durham, NH \r\n Skip to Main Content \r\n     Our Community   \t\t\t \n     Doing Business   \t\t\t \n     Inside Town Hall   \t\t\t \n     Helpful Resources   \t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t Search \n\t\t\t Upcoming Elections \r\n\t\t\t Polling Hours & Voting Location \r\n\t\t\t How to Register to Vote in Durham \r\n\t\t\t Student Voting \r\nHome \nInside Town Hall \nDepartments \nTown Clerk/Tax Collector \nVoting and Election Information \nStudent Voting \r\nStudent Voting\t\t \r\nRecent changes in NH Election law have made it more difficult to use a student ID as proof of identity. \nIf possible, bring one of the following with you when you register, and more importantly, when you go to vote: \nDriver’s license issued by any state or federal government \nNon-driver ID card issued by NH DMV or motor vehicle agency of another state \nPhoto ID card for “voting identification only” issued by NH DMV (RSA 260:21) \nUnited States armed services identification card \nUnited States passport or passcard \nUsing one of the above IDs will enable you to register more quickly and to avoid time-consuming extra steps when you vote. You may present photocopies or digital copies of any one of the above. \nIf you do not possess the above IDs and cannot obtain them before registering, you will still be able to register to vote if you can provide some other photo ID (e.g. student ID) and proof of your age. Proof of citizenship and domicile are also needed, but alternatives to providing them are easier than proving your identity or age. \nIf you use your student ID to prove your identity when registering, you must also present documentation to prove that you are 18 years of age or older. Using one of the photo IDs listed above enables you to prove both your identity and your age. \nBe aware that even after registering, in order to receive a ballot, you must show a photo ID.  If at all possible, present one of the approved IDs listed above. If you register prior to Election Day using an alternate form of ID, you may still have time to obtain one of the approved forms of ID . Presenting other forms of photo ID on Election Day will require you to getting additional verification which will be time-consuming for you, for election officials, and for your fellow voting citizens. \nFor a comprehensive description and further detail about what you need and how to register, see  How To Register To Vote in Durham  https://www.durhamnh.gov/705/How-to-Register-to-Vote-in-Durham   or the NH Secretary of State website   https://www.sos.nh.gov/elections/register-vote \n\t\t\t Town GIS Map \r\n\t\t\t Agendas & Minutes \r\n\t\t\t DCAT Media on Demand \r\n\t\t\t Online Payments \r\n\t\t\t Recreation \r\n\t\t\t Trash & Recycling \r\nContact Us \r\n8 Newmarket Rd \nDurham, NH 03824 \r\nPhone:  603-868-5571 \r\nQuick Links \r\n         Calendar \n         Directory \n         Subscribe \n         Welcome Visitors \n         Sustainable Durham \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\nSite Links \r\n         Home \n         Sign In \n         Site Map \n         Contact Us \n         Accessibility \n         Copyright Notices \n         Privacy Policy \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\n   Government Websites by  CivicPlus® \nLoading \r\n\t\t\t\tLoading\r\n\t\t\t Do Not Show Again \r\n\t\t\t Close \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Left \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Right \r\n[] \r\n                     Slideshow Left Arrow \r\n                     Slideshow Right Arrow \r\n ",
